  "correctAnswer": "B",
  "explanation": "Since the vertex is at $(0,-8)$, we have $f(0) = -8$. Substituting into $f(x) = ax^2 - k$ gives $-k = -8$, so $k = 8$. Thus $f(x) = ax^2 - 8$. Since the graph passes through $(2,-32)$, we have $4a - 8 = -32$, so $4a = -24$, giving $a = -6$.\n\nWhy C is incorrect:\n\nResults from an arithmetic error when solving $4a - 8 = -32$. Incorrectly calculating $-32 + 8 = -16$ instead of $-24$ gives $4a = -16$, leading to $a = -4$.",
